# Mechanics 03 — A sounding rocket: variable mass, gravity and air drag
#
# (Taylor, Classical Mechanics, §3.2; Kleppner & Kolenkow ch. 4.)
# A single-stage sounding rocket has lift-off mass m₀ = 1200 kg, of which
# 900 kg is propellant, burned at a constant rate over 60.0 s. The exhaust
# leaves at v_e = 2.20 km/s relative to the rocket. It is launched vertically.
#
#   (a) The Tsiolkovsky Δv (no gravity, no air) and the thrust.
#   (b) With uniform gravity g = 9.81 m/s² but no air: burnout speed and height
#       (closed form), and the highest point reached after coasting.
#   (c) Check (b) by solving m v' = v_e ṁ − m g.
#   (d) Add quadratic air drag, ½ ρ(y) C_d A v², in an exponential atmosphere
#       ρ(y) = 1.225 kg/m³ · exp(−y / 8.50 km), with C_d = 0.50 and a body
#       radius of 25.0 cm. Find the burnout speed, the burnout height and the
#       apex height.

m0 = 1200 kg
m_fuel = 900 kg
t_b = 60.0 s
v_e = 2.20 km/s
g = 9.81 m/s²

ṁ = m_fuel / t_b
m_f = m0 - m_fuel

# (a)
print "thrust:", v_e ṁ in kN to 6 digits
print "Tsiolkovsky Δv:", v_e ln(m0 / m_f) to 6 digits

# (b) closed form with gravity
v_b = v_e ln(m0 / m_f) - g t_b
y_b = v_e t_b - ½ g t_b² - v_e m_f / ṁ * ln(m0 / m_f)
print "burnout speed (no air):", v_b to 6 digits
print "burnout height (no air):", y_b in km to 6 digits
print "apex (no air):", (y_b + v_b² / (2*g)) in km to 6 digits

# (c) the same by ODE
solve M' = -ṁ,
      M v' = v_e ṁ - M g,
      y' = v
  with M(0) = m0, v(0) = 0 m/s, y(0) = 0 m
  for t from 0 s to t_b
print "ODE burnout speed (no air):", v(t_b) to 6 digits
print "ODE burnout height (no air):", y(t_b) in km to 6 digits

# (d) with drag. Powered phase first ...
C_d = 0.50
A = π (25.0 cm)²
ρ0 = 1.225 kg/m³
H = 8.50 km
ρ(z) = ρ0 exp(-z / H)
solve Mp' = -ṁ,
      Mp vp' = v_e ṁ - Mp g - ½ ρ(yp) C_d A vp |vp|,
      yp' = vp
  with Mp(0) = m0, vp(0) = 0 m/s, yp(0) = 0 m
  for t from 0 s to t_b
print "burnout speed (air):", vp(t_b) to 6 digits
print "burnout height (air):", yp(t_b) in km to 6 digits

# ... then coasting, starting from where the powered phase ended.
solve vc' = -g - ½ ρ(yc) C_d A vc |vc| / m_f,
      yc' = vc
  with vc(t_b) = vp(t_b), yc(t_b) = yp(t_b)
  for t from t_b to t_b + 400 s

# apex: the vertical speed is zero
solve vc(t_top) = 0 m/s for t_top from t_b to t_b + 400 s
print "time of apex (air):", t_top to 6 digits
print "apex (air):", yc(t_top) in km to 6 digits
